<title>USA: Catalina Lighting to appeal Browder verdict.</title>
<headline>Catalina Lighting to appeal Browder verdict.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Catalina Lighting Inc on Thursday said it would appeal the verdict returned against the company in a lawsuit brought by its former president, John Browder.</p>
<p>The suit arose out of the termination of Browder's employment  contract in April 1991. He was awarded $1.1 million for past salary and $400,000 for stock options.</p>
<p>The company said it thought the verdict was &quot;contrary to the weight of the evidence,&quot; and that it planned to seek a new trial.</p>
<p>Catalina makes products for the lighting industry.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
